---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<Base
  title="Methodology — How Our Predictions Are Made"
  description="How the site produces predictions: proprietary multi-source consensus, market-efficient price cross-checks, audited edges and public settlement records."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white">Methodology</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-slate-400">
      Every pick is generated by the same auditable process. Here is the level of detail we publish.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 p-5 rounded-xl border-2 border-brand-500/30 bg-brand-500/5">
      <p class="text-sm">
        <strong class="text-white">TL;DR:</strong> Predictions are produced by a proprietary consensus engine that cross-checks multiple independent signals — market prices, model outputs and expert opinion — and publishes only picks that clear a strict audited threshold. Every settled result is logged publicly. No cherry-picking.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-3">1. Multi-signal aggregation</h2>
    <p>
      Our pipeline ingests three broad classes of signal every cycle:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 mt-3">
      <li><strong class="text-white">Market-efficient prices</strong> — reference prices used by professional bettors to gauge where informed money actually goes.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-white">Statistical models</strong> — mechanical baselines calibrated on historical outcomes.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-white">Expert opinion</strong> — independent human-and-model tipster signals, weighted by their long-run performance on our own settled record.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-400">
      The specific data providers, sample sizes and weighting formulas are proprietary. Publishing them would let other operators copy our edge without doing the work — and it would let scrapers front-run our picks. What we <em>do</em> commit to is that every rule is deterministic, auditable, and settled from real results.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-3">2. Consensus — a pick has to earn its way in</h2>
    <p>
      Raw agreement between signals is not enough. A pick is only published when:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 mt-3">
      <li>A minimum number of <em>independent</em> signals agree on the selection.</li>
      <li>At least one of those signals has an audited positive ROI in the same odds band on our own settled record.</li>
      <li>The pick is not in a league or bracket where those signals are known to underperform.</li>
      <li>The live market price still represents value at publication time.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-3">3. Three disjoint tracked systems</h2>
    <p>
      Picks are sorted into exactly one of three feeds by their published odds:
    </p>
    <div class="grid gap-3 mt-4 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-sky-500/30 bg-sky-500/5">
        <p class="font-display font-bold text-sky-400">WIN</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">Favorites ≤ 1.80. Highest strike rate.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-brand-500/30 bg-brand-500/5">
        <p class="font-display font-bold text-brand-400">OVERALL</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">Value 2.60–3.49. Balanced ROI engine.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-gold/30 bg-gold/5">
        <p class="font-display font-bold text-gold">ROI / VIP</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">High value ≥ 3.50. Maximum return per unit.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-400">
      The three bands do NOT overlap. Every settled pick counts toward exactly one record. The 1.80–2.60 dead zone is skipped entirely — statistically nobody beats the market there. See <a class="text-brand-400 underline" href="/results">the live records</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-3">4. Settlement — real scores, cross-checked</h2>
    <p>
      When a match finishes, the final score is pulled from multiple independent resolvers and cross-checked. A dedicated reconciliation pass compares the stored score against the pick's outcome label; any disagreement is logged and corrected. The full conflict log is published to keep us honest.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-3">5. Ratings — everything is audited</h2>
    <p>
      Every internal signal is scored on ROI (not win-rate) over our real settled record. Signals that stop earning are demoted or dropped. Signals that consistently earn get more weight. There is no hidden model — the ratings themselves are deterministic, and a new set is produced every cycle from the current settled record.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-3">6. Transparency guarantees</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 mt-3">
      <li><strong class="text-white">Flat 1u stakes</strong> — every pick, every band. No stake-sizing that flatters the past.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-white">No losers deleted</strong> — every settled pick lives forever on <a class="text-brand-400 underline" href="/results">/results</a>. Wins and losses.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-white">Closing Line Value tracked</strong> — the % of our picks that beat the market's closing line — a stronger long-term signal than a hot streak.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-white">GENESIS date locked</strong> — the /results record starts at a fixed date; earlier picks are archived separately so no rule change silently rewrites history.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-3">Not a crystal ball</h2>
    <p class="text-slate-400">
      No system predicts sport perfectly. Even our best band loses roughly one bet in two — the profit comes from betting at prices that pay more than the loss rate implies. Bet only what you can afford to lose. If gambling is affecting your life, our <a class="text-brand-400 underline" href="/responsible-gambling">responsible-gambling page</a> lists free confidential help. {SITE.minAge}+.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
